 BiomeGenBase but climate never selects it; b1.7.3 has no ravines.
 
 ## Changelog
+- `done` milestone 6 of the Photon port: GTAO, water + translucent layer, weather (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +3 tests not run: `gtao::shader_text_is_complete`, `water::water_text_and_pack`, `weather::rain_columns_and_gaussian`; the last compares `JavaRandom::next_gaussian` with the JDK value for seed 42 from memory):
+    - `render/gtao.rs`: `d3_ao.fsh` + `gtao.glsl` + slerp/catmull-rom/r2, half resolution, temporal accumulation, ping-pong history. Outputs `ambient` (ao, SSS, bent normal xy) and `history_data` (1 - depth, age); `AO_UPSAMPLE_WGSL` is `d4_deferred_shading`'s depth-aware upsample for milestone 1 to paste. Normal rebuilt from depth until the G-buffer exists (marked `ponytail:`). Not wired into `lib.rs`: nothing reads it yet.
+    - `render/water.rs`: `gbuffers_all_translucent` water path (Gerstner waves, height variation, parallax, `get_water_displacement` in the vertex stage, texture + edge highlight, `water_fog_simple` absorption, GGX sun/moon highlight, diffuse) into a translucent layer with its own depth + a refraction target, then `c1_blend_layers` (refraction + `scene * (1 - a) + rgb`). Needs a scene colour texture that is not the target (milestone 1's HDR buffer) and a stored opaque depth. Missing, all because the input is milestone 2/3/4/5's: sky and environment reflections, PCSS shadows (uses the pack's no-shadow `pow8(skylight)`), cloud shadows, `common_fog`/analytic fog (uses the chunk shader's terrain fog), Purkinje shift. Sky/ambient colours are uniforms (`Frame`).
+    - `render/weather.rs`: `EntityRenderer.renderRainSnow` geometry (same Random draws, quads, alpha, light; radius 5, `FANCY` false) + `gbuffers_weather` shading (slanted rain, `RAIN_OPACITY` 0.25, `SNOW_OPACITY` 0.75, premultiplied) drawn inside the water pass. Support: `JavaRandom::next_gaussian`, `ChunkManager::biomes` / `top_solid`, `Biome::snows` / `rains`, `assets/rain.rgba`, `assets/snow.rgba` (from the jar's `environment/`), `assets/noise.rgba` (photon `noise.png`, `render/noise.rs`).
+    - Integration order (milestone 1 owns the frame graph): terrain pass into the HDR target with depth stored; `Gtao::run`; `WaterLayer::update/prepare/begin/setup`, draw water ranges, `Weather::update/draw`; `composite` into the next target. Old `fs_water` / `water_pipeline` in `gpu/pipeline.rs` and the packed water column in `mesh.rs` become dead then.
+- `done` Photon rewrite, milestone 5: the post chain (written on a Linux host: `render/post.rs` compiled, its 3 tests pass, the chain ran headless on lavapipe in 4 configurations x 4 frames; the `lib.rs` wiring is NOT compiled, nothing ran on a device; no FPS numbers):
+    - `render/post.rs` + `render/post.wgsl` (new, + `assets/noise_b.r8` = `noise.png`'s blue channel for DOF): port of Photon `c2_dof`, `c4_taa_exposure` (TAA with variance + AABB clipping, closest-fragment reprojection, catmull-rom history, off-centre rejection, auto exposure off / simple / histogram), `c5`..`c10` bloom down, `c11` merge, `c12`/`c13` gaussian, `c14`..`c18` up, `c19_color_grading` (bloom mix, exposure, vignette, grade in/out, white balance, tonemap, every operator of `tonemap_operators.glsl` incl. ACES full + fit), `c21_fxaa`, `final` (CAS, dither). `Settings::default()` = `settings.glsl` defaults; the tonemap is ACES full (the pack ships Lottes: `Tonemap::Lottes`).
+    - `lib.rs`: the chunk/sky/entity/water pass draws into `Post::scene_view()` with the jittered projection (`Post::jittered`), `vl::composite` now blends into that scene (own pass) instead of the surface, `Post::draw` ends on the surface, the HUD pass draws last (not tonemapped). The depth buffer is now always stored (TAA and DOF read it). `Gpu::resize` is followed by `Post::resize`.
+    - Same maths, different plumbing: y-down uv, depth 0..1, Iris' colortex0 flip is two explicit bloom textures with the same read/write order (so photon's quirk that tiles 3 and 1 read the horizontally-blurred copy as destination is kept), exposure is a 1x1 pass (also keeps `centerDepthSmooth`), matrices of `color.glsl`/`aces` are multiplied in f64 and written as literals, `texelFetch` is clamped to the edge. Jitter keeps the pack's `jitter_y / viewWidth`.
+    - Not ported: TAAU + `c3_taau_prep` (render scale 1), motion blur `c20`, `BLOOMY_FOG` (needs the fog buffer of milestone 4), debug views. ponytail: sky and the volumetric march use the unjittered camera (<= 0.33 px), the scene is stored in the surface format until the G-buffer milestone makes it HDR (until then `exposure` 1 + ACES darken the old LDR frame), no hand (`HAND_DEPTH` only matches within ~0.11 block), exposure reads the scene before DOF, 20 small passes per frame (first lever for a low-end GPU: `Settings.bloom = false`, then `fxaa`).
+    - UNVERIFIED on a device: look and cost; sRGB-surface handling (`final` undoes the hardware encode because the pack writes display-encoded values).
+- `done` photon port, milestone 3 of 6: shadows (photon `include/lighting/shadows/{common,distortion,pcss}.glsl` + the distortion of `program/shadow.vsh`; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, +3 tests not run; the lookup maths was checked in a numpy transcription of the GLSL, see below):
+    - `render/shadows.rs` (new): `distortion_wgsl()` (quartic distortion `SHADOW_DISTORTION` 0.85, `SHADOW_DEPTH_SCALE` 0.2, `get_shadow_bias`) and `pcss_wgsl()` (`blocker_search`, `shadow_pcf`, `get_filtered_shadows`, `get_shadow_distance_fade`, `get_lightmap_shadows`, `get_lightmap_light_leak_prevention`) as WGSL; `Shadows` = group 2 (`ShadowU`: `shadowModelView` in scene space, GL `shadowProjection`, light, eye, frame; `noisetex`). photon "medium" profile: `SHADOW_PCF` + `SHADOW_VPS`, no `SHADOW_COLOR` (needs the M6 translucent pass), no `SHADOW_SSRT` (needs the M1 G-buffer): past the map `get_lightmap_shadows`. `assets/noise_b.r8` + `tools/gen_noise.py` = the pack's `noisetex.b` (blue noise).
+    - `gpu/pipeline.rs`: `vs_shadow` uses `distort_shadow_space`, stored depth is `z_gl * 0.1 + 0.5`; the comparison sampler is linear (`shadowHardwareFiltering1`); `Uniforms.sh`, `SHADOW_DISTORT`, `SHADOW_BIAS`, `SHADOW_BRIGHTNESS` are gone. `render/camera.rs`: `shadow_view`, `shadow_model_view`, `shadow_projection` (the pack's split of the same box); `shadow_view_proj` is unchanged (culling, `vs_shadow`).
+    - `render/vl.rs` (volumetric light kept, only its lookups moved): the march distorts like the shadow pass (`DEPTH_BIAS` = 0.25 block in the new depth units); the surface shadow is `get_filtered_shadows` mixed with `get_lightmap_shadows` by `distance_fade` (as `d4_deferred_shading.fsh`), replacing the hand-made normal offset, slope bias, 4 extra depth taps and the grazing fade (`NORMAL_BIAS`, `SH_RES` deleted). Entity map: `shadowtex0` = min of both depths, `shadowtex1` = min of both compares.
+    - Deviations: back-face culling stays (the pack's `shadow.culling = reversed` would erase the sun-facing hull, the mesher drops hidden faces); `frameCounter` is 0 until TAA (M5, const `TAA`); skylight 1, no clouds, no SSS until M1/M4; foliage is still parked by tile in `vs_shadow` (photon's `shadow.fsh` alpha discard + colour output belong with M6); 1024^2 over 64 blocks = the pack's 8 texels per block.
+    - Check done off-device: numpy transcription of the GLSL lookups against a rasterised map (per-vertex distortion, back-face culled): flat ground at sun 10..88 degrees and eye offsets, 0..90 blocks: lit 1.000 (min 1.00, no acne); sun-facing wall at 25/35/60 degrees: 1.000; pillar umbra 0.001; with the bias off the same ground is 0.563 lit. UNVERIFIED on a device: that the WGSL compiles (no validator was available), PCSS grain after the 4-tap blur, cost of the half-resolution PCSS on low-end GPUs (`SHADOW_PCF_STEPS_MAX`, `SSS_STEPS`, `SHADOW_VPS` are the levers).
+- `done` Photon port, milestone 2 of 6: sky (d0 sky map, d4a sky SH, stars, sun, moon; written WITHOUT an Android build: `render/sky.rs` and both shaders compiled and ran headless on lavapipe, 2 tests pass; `lib.rs` NOT compiled (`ndk-sys` only builds for Android), its 4 edits are read by eye; not run on a device). Photon Shaders by SixthSurge, licence in `LICENSE-PHOTON` (no redistribution on platforms that pay creators, no selling):
+    - `render/sky.wgsl` = `atmosphere.glsl` (LUT lookup for sun and moon together, analytic transmittance), `light_color.glsl`, `weather_color.glsl`, `projection.glsl`, `stars.glsl`, the sun and moon of `sky.glsl`, `d0_sky_map`, SH helpers. `render/sky_sh.wgsl` = `d4a_generate_sky_sh`. `assets/scattering.dat` is the pack's `scattering.dat` unchanged (RGB16F, padded to RGBA at load), `assets/noise.rgba` its `noise.png` (`tools/gen_noise.py`).
+    - `render/sky.rs`: `SkyRenderer::encode` (sky map 192x108 rgba16f, light/ambient colour in column 191, then the SH) before the scene, `draw` over every pixel still at depth 1 after the opaque draws. `params` turns mc-rs's sun angle into the pack's uniforms (`sunAngle = fract(angle + 0.25)`, rising half = `angle > 0.5`, no moon phases in b1.7.3). The vanilla dome, sunrise fan, sun/moon quads, glare and star quads are gone (`world::sky::star_vertices` etc. stay, golden-tested, unused by the renderer).
+    - For milestone 1 (d4): `sky::WGSL` is the library (`draw_sky`, `atmosphere_scattering`, `project_sky`, `sh_evaluate_irradiance`), `sky_map`, `sh` (9 coefficients + irradiance up, vec4 each), `bind_group()`/`layout`.
+    - Deviations: SH is one 64-thread group of 4 samples (same 256 samples; the pack's 27 KB of shared memory exceeds the 16 KB limit) and goes to a buffer, not column 191. Not in yet: clouds and aurora (M4; aurora is in no milestone), analytic fog over the sky map (M4), rainbow and snow/sand weather colour (M6). `stand_in_tonemap` (fixed exposure + ACES fit) is temporary: delete with M5.
+    - Known until M4: terrain fog still fades to the vanilla horizon colour, which differs from the new horizon.
+- `done` photon port, milestone 1: G-buffer + deferred lighting into the HDR frame (its own tone map + grade were dropped when M5 landed: `render/post.rs` owns the HDR scene and the swap-chain output; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +2 tests in `render/photon.rs` not run, `mesh`/`chunks` tests edited for the new stride). Ported from `photon-main`: `d4_deferred_shading.fsh` (terrain branch), `diffuse_lighting.glsl`, `light_color.glsl`, `atmosphere.glsl` (analytic transmittance, sun+moon LUT mapping, post-processing), `d0_sky_map.vsh` `get_ambient_color`, `c19_color_grading.fsh` (grade_input, `tonemap_lottes`, grade_output, vignette) and the `AUTO_EXPOSURE_OFF` exposure of `c4_taa_exposure.vsh`. `render/vl.rs` is kept: it still marches the shafts and its green channel is now the surface shadow the deferred pass reads; its blend no longer darkens the frame (`res.w` = 0) and is drawn in the HDR pass.
+    - Frame: G-buffer pass (terrain, items, outline: albedo + `face * 256 + lm` in an RGBA16F target, depth kept) -> `vl` march (now every frame) -> HDR scene pass (sky, `fs_deferred`, water, shafts) -> tone map into the swap chain under the HUD. `Vertex` gains `lm` (`sky * 16 + block`, raw sky light, `mesh::VF` = 7 floats); `light` stays for water depth. The `lighting()` colours (`light_color`, `ambient_color`, `blocklight_color`, `time_noon`) are computed on the CPU from the pack's `scattering.dat` (`assets/scattering.dat`).
+    - Deviations: the sky pass is still mc-rs's (LDR colours in the HDR frame); ambient is the pack's non-SH branch (`ambient_color * sqr(sky)`); no AO, SSS, cloud shadows, bent normals, coloured lights, handheld light; shadow = the half-resolution one from `vl` (no PCSS/SSRT); direct light x `1 - 0.9 rain` stands in for cloud shadows; flat normal from `dpdx`/`dpdy`; items/mobs/outline are lit as sky level 15; fog is still AstraLex's, now applied in the deferred pass and in `fs_water`.
+    - Not done (next milestones): 2 sky (`d0`, `d4a` SH, stars), 3 shadows (`d4` PCSS + SSRT), 4 fog + clouds (`d1`, `d2`, `p0`), 5 post (TAA + exposure, bloom, DOF, FXAA, white balance), 6 GTAO, water/translucents, weather. Skipped for good: LPV, Photonics, LoD-mod support.
 - `done` shadow cone: the umbra an item or mob throws through the air, from the object to the ground (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; no test, the logic is a draw call and two constants; no FPS numbers):
     - `gpu/pipeline.rs` `vs_cone`/`fs_cone` + `cone_pipeline`, `lib.rs` `CONE_COPIES`: after the entity mesh (and before the water), the same buffer is drawn `CONE_COPIES` (40) more times as instances 1..=40, each slid `CONE_STEP` (0.2 block) further from the sun (`u.sun.xyz` is the direction toward it), as a black layer of alpha `CONE_ALPHA` (0.04) x shadow strength, both faces, depth test on, no depth write. Along a view ray the layers stack with the path through the swept volume (about 10% seen across a 0.25 item, up to ~95% looking straight along the light), and the ground cuts the cone where it lands. It is Minkowski-sum-by-instancing, no silhouette maths.
     - Knobs: `CONE_ALPHA` is the darkness, `CONE_STEP` x `CONE_COPIES` the reach. Ceilings (ponytail): a tall mob under a low sun has a longer umbra than 8 blocks and is cut short; every copy draws the whole entity buffer (fill cost scales with copies x entities on screen); the cone is a parallel prism, a point light like the diagram's would need a per-copy scale.
